<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 23 January, from 1368 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1368</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhu Yuanzhang proclaims the Ming dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former peasant and rebel leader declared himself the Hongwu Emperor at Nanjing. The Ming drove out the Mongol Yuan and ruled China for 276 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Hongwu Emperor</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1556</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Shaanxi earthquake, the deadliest on record, strikes China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake centred in the Wei River valley killed an estimated 830,000 people. Many died when cave dwellings carved into soft loess cliffs collapsed.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1849</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth Blackwell becomes the first woman to earn a US medical degree</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Admitted to Geneva Medical College in New York almost as a joke, Blackwell graduated top of her class. She went on to found hospitals and a medical college for women.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1920</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Netherlands refuses to hand over Kaiser Wilhelm II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dutch government rejected Allied demands to extradite the former German Emperor for trial under the Treaty of Versailles. Wilhelm lived in exile at Doorn until his death in 1941.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1943</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British Eighth Army captures Tripoli</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Montgomery's troops entered Tripoli, three months after El Alamein, as Rommel's forces retreated into Tunisia. It ended Italy's North African empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1968</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">North Korea seizes the USS Pueblo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">North Korean vessels captured the US Navy intelligence ship off Wonsan, killing one sailor. The 82 surviving crew were held for eleven months, and the ship is still held in Pyongyang.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></li></ol>
